.TH "ROARK\-INTEGRATIONS\-CALENDAR\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-integrations-calendar-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-integrations\-calendar\-create \- Connect a calendar account
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark integrations calendar create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Verifies the credential against the provider and, only if it works, stores it encrypted. A credential the provider rejects is a 400 and no connection is created: a connection that has never worked would next be exercised by an inbound call at 2am, with nobody there to fix it.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/integrations/calendar
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fI<value>\fR
Who holds the calendar. CAL_COM is connected with an API key; GOOGLE is connected by consent, through `POST /v1/integrations/calendar/google/authorize\-url`. CALENDLY is described by `capabilities` but not yet connectable. One of: CAL_COM, GOOGLE, CALENDLY. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<value>\fR
Customer\-facing name for this account, unique within the project. Required. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<value>\fR
The provider account’s API key. For CAL_COM, a Cal.com API key (starts with `cal_`). It is verified against the provider before anything is stored, so an invalid key is a 400 and no connection is created. Stored encrypted and never returned. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-timezone\fR \fI<value>\fR
The named IANA timezone to offer slots in, for example `America/Los_Angeles`. Omit to adopt the provider account’s own timezone. A fixed offset such as `\-08:00` is rejected: it does not observe DST. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
